CHANGED FC2-c030 {"id": "FC2-c030", "lesson": "L02", "front": "With a lending rate r_ℓ at most a borrowing rate r_b, which forward prices admit arbitrage?", "back": "Under A1 and A3, with A4 at the two rates in place of r, and the frictionless parts of A2 (no transaction costs, free short sales, unrestricted lending and borrowing, and no default risk), a price F outside [S e^{r_ℓ τ}, S e^{r_b τ}] admits arbitrage when r_ℓ ≤ r_b (Problem R1). The lesson does not prove that every price inside the interval is arbitrage-free.", "grade": "T", "basis": "Problem R1 (exact)"}
